From 1de1c36e12f7621c7f8972dc3d83bc5af9a8e650 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: anyingiit <49945850+anyingiit@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 21:22:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Keep an exited terminal's auto-derived tab name across a
 restart
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A terminal whose shell had exited before the editor quit came back as
`*Terminal N* (exited)` instead of `bash — <cwd> (exited)`: only explicit
titles were saved, and an auto-named tab re-derives its name from the
live process after restore, which a restored dead terminal doesn't have.
Two dead shells from different directories then looked the same (#3074).

Keep the name an auto-named tab had derived when its process quit on the
exited record, save it in the workspace's exited-terminal state, and put
it back on the restored dead tab. The tab stays auto-named, so a restart
still re-derives the name from the new process.

Fixes #3074

Assisted-by: Claude Code
